      <!-- SECURITY -->
      <div class="content-card" id="c2-security">
        <h2><div class="section-icon icon-yellow">🔒</div> Domain 2: Security (25%)</h2>

        <h3>Malware Types</h3>
        <table class="data-table">
          <tr><th>Malware</th><th>How It Works</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Virus</td><td>Attaches to files, spreads when file is executed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Worm</td><td>Self-replicates across network WITHOUT user action</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Trojan</td><td>Disguised as legitimate software — creates backdoor</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ransomware</td><td>Encrypts files, demands payment for key</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Spyware</td><td>Secretly monitors and reports user activity</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Adware</td><td>Displays unwanted ads, often bundled with free software</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Rootkit</td><td>Hides itself in OS, gives admin access to attacker</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Keylogger</td><td>Records keystrokes to steal passwords</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Botnet</td><td>Network of infected machines controlled remotely</td></tr>
        </table>

        <h3>Social Engineering Attacks</h3>
        <div class="must-know">
          <div class="must-know-header">⚠️ MUST KNOW — Social Engineering Types</div>
          <p>• <strong>Phishing</strong> — Fake email that tricks you into revealing credentials or clicking malicious links</p>
          <p>• <strong>Spear phishing</strong> — Targeted phishing aimed at specific individual/organization</p>
          <p>• <strong>Whaling</strong> — Phishing targeting executives (C-level)</p>
          <p>• <strong>Vishing</strong> — Voice phishing — phone call scam</p>
          <p>• <strong>Smishing</strong> — SMS phishing — text message scam</p>
          <p>• <strong>Tailgating/Piggybacking</strong> — Following someone through a secure door</td></p>
          <p>• <strong>Shoulder surfing</strong> — Watching someone enter passwords</p>
          <p>• <strong>Dumpster diving</strong> — Finding sensitive info in trash</p>
          <p>• <strong>Pretexting</strong> — Creating a fake scenario to manipulate someone</p>
        </div>

        <h3>Authentication Methods</h3>
        <table class="data-table">
          <tr><th>Factor</th><th>Type</th><th>Examples</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Something you know</td><td>Knowledge</td><td>Password, PIN, security question</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Something you have</td><td>Possession</td><td>Smart card, token, phone (TOTP)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Something you are</td><td>Biometric</td><td>Fingerprint, face, iris, retina</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Somewhere you are</td><td>Location</td><td>GPS location, network location</td></tr>
          <tr><td>MFA</td><td>Multi-Factor</td><td>Combines 2+ of the above</td></tr>
        </table>

        <h3>Encryption & Security Tools</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>BitLocker:</strong> Windows full-disk encryption (Pro/Enterprise required)</li>
          <li><strong>FileVault:</strong> macOS full-disk encryption</li>
          <li><strong>EFS (Encrypting File System):</strong> NTFS-level file encryption (Pro+)</li>
          <li><strong>TPM (Trusted Platform Module):</strong> Hardware chip that stores encryption keys securely — required for BitLocker</li>
          <li><strong>VPN:</strong> Encrypts traffic over public networks — tunnel to private network</li>
          <li><strong>TLS/SSL:</strong> Encrypts web traffic (HTTPS)</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="must-know">
          <div class="must-know-header">⚠️ MUST KNOW — Windows Security Features</div>
          <p>• <strong>Windows Defender:</strong> Built-in antivirus/anti-malware</p>
          <p>• <strong>Windows Firewall:</strong> Built-in host-based firewall</p>
          <p>• <strong>UAC (User Account Control):</strong> Prompts for admin approval before system changes</p>
          <p>• <strong>Windows Hello:</strong> Biometric/PIN authentication for Windows login</p>
          <p>• <strong>Secure Boot:</strong> UEFI feature — blocks unsigned bootloaders (anti-rootkit)</p>
          <p>• <strong>Principle of least privilege:</strong> Give users ONLY the access they need</p>
        </div>

        <h3>Physical Security</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Mantrap:</strong> Two-door entry — one opens only when other closes</li>
          <li><strong>Badge/key card:</strong> RFID-based access control</li>
          <li><strong>Biometric locks:</strong> Fingerprint, retinal scan</li>
          <li><strong>Cable lock:</strong> Kensington lock — physically secures laptops</li>
          <li><strong>Privacy screen:</strong> Limits viewing angle to prevent shoulder surfing</li>
          <li><strong>Faraday cage:</strong> Blocks all electromagnetic signals</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Wireless Security</h3>
        <table class="data-table">
          <tr><th>Protocol</th><th>Security</th><th>Status</th></tr>
          <tr><td>WEP</td><td>Very weak (RC4)</td><td>Deprecated — DO NOT USE</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WPA</td><td>TKIP encryption</td><td>Deprecated</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WPA2</td><td>AES/CCMP encryption</td><td>Current standard (Personal + Enterprise)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WPA3</td><td>SAE — stronger handshake</td><td>Newest — most secure</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- SOFTWARE TROUBLESHOOTING -->
      <div class="content-card" id="c2-software">
        <h2><div class="section-icon icon-purple">⚙️</div> Domain 3: Software Troubleshooting (22%)</h2>

        <h3>Windows Troubleshooting Tools</h3>
        <table class="data-table">
          <tr><th>Tool</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Safe Mode</td><td>Boot with minimal drivers — diagnose driver/malware issues</td></tr>
          <tr><td>System Restore</td><td>Roll back system to previous working state</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Windows Recovery Environment (WinRE)</td><td>Advanced repair tools outside Windows</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Startup Repair</td><td>Automatically fixes common boot problems</td></tr>
          <tr><td>sfc /scannow</td><td>Repairs corrupted system files</td></tr>
          <tr><td>DISM /RestoreHealth</td><td>Repairs Windows image — use before sfc if needed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Memory Diagnostic</td><td>Tests RAM for errors — mdsched.exe</td></tr>
