  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A user reports the PC shuts off randomly and the case is very hot. What is the MOST likely cause?',options:['Failing PSU','Virus infection','Insufficient RAM','Overheating due to dust-clogged fans'],answer:3,explanation:'Thermal shutdown is a safety feature to prevent CPU/GPU damage. Dust-clogged fans and heatsinks are the most common cause of overheating in consumer PCs. Clean with compressed air.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'What does POST stand for?',options:['Power-On Self Test','Power Output System Test','Primary Operating System Test','Peripheral Output System Test'],answer:0,explanation:'POST (Power-On Self Test) is a diagnostic test run by the BIOS/UEFI firmware immediately when the computer is powered on. It checks that essential hardware (RAM, CPU, keyboard) is working.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'Which bus standard is used to connect graphics cards in modern motherboards?',options:['PCI','AGP','PCIe x16','ISA'],answer:2,explanation:'PCIe x16 (PCI Express x16) is the standard slot for graphics cards in modern motherboards, providing 16 lanes of bandwidth — far more than older AGP or PCI standards.'},
