  {domain:'🔧 Troubleshooting',q:'A laser printer is smearing toner on the printed page. What component is MOST likely faulty?',options:['Drum','Toner cartridge','Fuser','Transfer roller'],answer:2,explanation:'The fuser applies heat and pressure to bond toner permanently to paper. If the fuser is failing (temperature too low or roller damaged), toner will smear when touched.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Which protocol resolves domain names to IP addresses?',options:['DHCP','DNS','FTP','NAT'],answer:1,explanation:'DNS (Domain Name System) resolves human-readable domain names (like google.com) to IP addresses. It uses port 53 and uses both TCP and UDP.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'What is the purpose of a default gateway?',options:['Assigns IP addresses','Translates domain names','Routes traffic to other networks','Filters malicious traffic'],answer:2,explanation:'The default gateway is the router IP address that devices send traffic to when the destination is outside the local network. Without it, devices cannot reach the internet or other subnets.'},
  {domain:'📱 Mobile Devices',q:'Which Apple connector has been replaced by USB-C on newer iPhone models?',options:['Micro-USB','Mini-USB','Lightning','Thunderbolt 2'],answer:2,explanation:'Apple used the Lightning connector on iPhones and iPads for over a decade before transitioning to USB-C starting with the iPhone 15. USB-C is now the universal standard.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A technician needs to prevent accidental damage from static electricity when handling RAM. What should they use?',options:['Rubber gloves','Anti-static wrist strap','Cotton gloves','Nitrile gloves'],answer:1,explanation:'An anti-static wrist strap (ESD wrist strap) grounds the technician to the chassis, safely dissipating any static charge before it can damage sensitive components.'},
