  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'A network uses the address 10.0.0.0/8. How many host bits are available?',options:['8','16','24','32'],answer:2,explanation:'/8 means 8 network bits, leaving 32-8=24 host bits. This is a Class A private network with approximately 16 million usable host addresses.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Which port does Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) use?',options:['22','443','3389','8080'],answer:2,explanation:'RDP (Remote Desktop Protocol) uses port 3389. It allows remote control of Windows desktops and is Windows-native. SSH uses port 22.'},
