  {domain:'📱 Mobile Devices',q:'Which display type is known for true blacks and high contrast but has risk of burn-in?',options:['IPS','TN','VA','OLED'],answer:3,explanation:'OLED (Organic LED) turns off pixels completely for black, achieving infinite contrast. The organic compounds can degrade unevenly (burn-in) if static images are displayed for long periods.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'What does VLAN stand for and what is its primary benefit?',options:['Virtual LAN — logical network segmentation','Variable LAN — variable speed networking','Virtual Link Access Network — wireless extension','Verified Local Area Node — security verification'],answer:0,explanation:'VLAN (Virtual LAN) allows logical separation of network segments on the same physical switch. Benefits include security (isolating departments), traffic management, and reduced broadcast domains.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A user wants maximum storage redundancy AND performance. Which RAID level is BEST?',options:['RAID 0','RAID 1','RAID 5','RAID 10'],answer:3,explanation:'RAID 10 (1+0) combines RAID 1 mirroring with RAID 0 striping, providing both excellent performance and high redundancy. It requires a minimum of 4 drives.'},
