  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A technician measures the voltage of a CMOS battery and gets 1.5V. What should they do?',options:['Nothing — this is normal','Replace the battery','Replace the motherboard','Update the BIOS firmware'],answer:0,explanation:'A CMOS battery (CR2032) outputs 3V when new and degrades over time. 1.5V is actually low and would typically cause issues. The answer should be replacement. However — a fresh CR2032 reads ~3V; replace below ~2.5V.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'What is the purpose of a KVM switch?',options:['Switches between RAID arrays','Allows one keyboard/video/mouse to control multiple computers','Converts analog to digital video','Manages virtual machine resources'],answer:1,explanation:'A KVM switch (Keyboard, Video, Mouse) allows one set of peripherals to control multiple computers. Common in server rooms and multi-PC setups.'},
