  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'A company needs to allow remote employees to securely connect to the corporate network over the internet. What technology should be used?',options:['NAT','VLAN','VPN','DMZ'],answer:2,explanation:'A VPN (Virtual Private Network) creates an encrypted tunnel over the public internet, allowing remote workers to securely access corporate resources as if they were on the local network.'},
  {domain:'☁️ Virtualization',q:'Which cloud characteristic allows resources to be automatically scaled up or down based on demand?',options:['Resource pooling','On-demand self-service','Rapid elasticity','Broad network access'],answer:2,explanation:'Rapid elasticity (or scalability) allows cloud resources to be scaled up or down quickly and automatically, matching demand without manual intervention or overprovisioning.'},
  {domain:'🔧 Troubleshooting',q:'A user reports their printer is printing blank pages. The printer is an inkjet. What should the technician do FIRST?',options:['Replace the ink cartridge','Clean the print heads','Reinstall the printer driver','Replace the printer'],answer:1,explanation:'Inkjet printers commonly print blank pages due to clogged print heads. Running the print head cleaning utility from the printer software is the best first step.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Which fiber optic type uses a yellow jacket and is used for long-distance runs?',options:['Multi-mode','Single-mode','Plenum','Armored'],answer:1,explanation:'Single-mode fiber (SMF) has a yellow jacket and uses a laser light source for very long distances (kilometers). Multi-mode fiber (MMF) has an orange or aqua jacket and is used for shorter distances.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'Which memory technology corrects single-bit errors and detects double-bit errors, commonly used in servers?',options:['DDR5','SO-DIMM','ECC','Dual-channel'],answer:2,explanation:'ECC (Error-Correcting Code) RAM detects and corrects single-bit memory errors automatically, preventing crashes and data corruption. It is required in servers and workstations where reliability is critical.'},
  {domain:'🔧 Troubleshooting',q:'A user complains that the laptop screen is very dim, but connecting an external monitor shows a normal image. What has MOST likely failed?',options:['GPU','LCD panel','Backlight or inverter','Video cable'],answer:2,explanation:'If the GPU is working (external monitor fine) but the laptop screen is dim, the backlight (LED) or inverter (CCFL screens) has failed. The LCD panel itself may be functional.'},
  {domain:'📱 Mobile Devices',q:'A user wants to sync emails to their mobile device so that deleting on the phone also deletes on the server. Which protocol should be configured?',options:['POP3','SMTP','IMAP','ActiveSync'],answer:2,explanation:'IMAP (port 143) keeps email on the server and syncs across all devices — delete on one device and it\'s deleted everywhere. POP3 downloads and typically removes from the server.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Port 53 is associated with which protocol?',options:['DHCP','DNS','SMTP','HTTP'],answer:1,explanation:'DNS (Domain Name System) uses port 53 for both UDP (most queries) and TCP (large responses and zone transfers). It is one of the most fundamental internet protocols.'},
  {domain:'☁️ Virtualization',q:'Which virtual machine feature allows you to save the entire state of a VM and revert to it later?',options:['Live migration','Cloning','Snapshot','Checkpoint'],answer:2,explanation:'A snapshot captures the complete state of a VM — RAM, disk, CPU state — at a specific point in time. You can revert to it if changes cause problems. (Note: Checkpoint is Microsoft\'s term for snapshot in Hyper-V.)'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A technician wants to use cable management best practices. Which SATA cable connects storage devices to the motherboard?',options:['15-pin SATA power','7-pin SATA data','Molex 4-pin','PCIe 8-pin'],answer:1,explanation:'The 7-pin SATA data cable connects the storage device to the motherboard SATA port. The 15-pin SATA power cable from the PSU provides power. Both are needed.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Which wireless security protocol is considered BROKEN and should NEVER be used?',options:['WPA2','WPA3','WPA','WEP'],answer:3,explanation:'WEP (Wired Equivalent Privacy) was cracked in 2001 and can be broken in minutes with freely available tools. WPA2-AES is the current standard; WPA3 is the newest.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A technician notices a yellow exclamation mark next to a device in Device Manager. What does this indicate?',options:['The device is disabled','The device has a driver problem','The device is updating','The device is a removable device'],answer:1,explanation:'A yellow exclamation mark (!) in Device Manager indicates a device driver error — either missing, corrupted, or conflicting driver. Right-clicking and selecting Update Driver is the first step.'},
  {domain:'🔧 Troubleshooting',q:'Which RAID level has NO redundancy and will lose all data if one drive fails?',options:['RAID 1','RAID 5','RAID 0','RAID 6'],answer:2,explanation:'RAID 0 (striping) has zero fault tolerance. It improves performance by splitting data across drives, but one drive failure destroys all data. It is NOT safe for critical data.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Which tool would you use to test if a network port is passing traffic without connecting to the network?',options:['Cable tester','Toner probe','Loopback plug','Multimeter'],answer:2,explanation:'A loopback plug creates a loop back through the RJ-45 port, allowing the NIC to send and receive to itself. This tests if the port hardware is functional without needing a live network connection.'},
  {domain:'📱 Mobile Devices',q:'What does MDM stand for in the context of enterprise mobile device management?',options:['Mobile Data Management','Mobile Device Management','Main Desktop Module','Managed Device Mode'],answer:1,explanation:'MDM (Mobile Device Management) is software that allows IT administrators to manage, monitor, secure, and enforce policies on employee mobile devices remotely.'},
  {domain:'☁️ Virtualization',q:'Which cloud model is dedicated to a single organization and hosted either on-premises or by a third party?',options:['Public','Private','Hybrid','Community'],answer:1,explanation:'A private cloud is dedicated to one organization, offering more control and security. It can be hosted on-premises or by a provider who maintains dedicated infrastructure just for that customer.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'What type of connector does a standard desktop ATX power supply use to power the motherboard?',options:['8-pin EPS','24-pin ATX','6-pin PCIe','4-pin Molex'],answer:1,explanation:'The main motherboard power connector is the 24-pin ATX connector. The CPU requires an additional 4 or 8-pin EPS connector. Graphics cards use 6 or 8-pin PCIe connectors.'},
  {domain:'🔧 Troubleshooting',q:'A user reports that a laser printer leaves toner on the page but it rubs off easily. Which component should be replaced?',options:['Toner cartridge','Drum','Fuser','Transfer belt'],answer:2,explanation:'Toner that rubs off easily has not been fused properly. The fuser applies heat and pressure to permanently bond toner to paper. A failing fuser (not hot enough) causes this exact symptom.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Which device connects a LAN to the internet and typically provides NAT?',options:['Switch','Hub','Router','Access Point'],answer:2,explanation:'A router connects different networks — typically the home/office LAN to the internet. It also performs NAT (Network Address Translation), allowing multiple devices to share one public IP address.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A user wants to add a second monitor to their workstation. The GPU has one HDMI and one DisplayPort output. Both displays support both connectors. What should they do?',options:['Buy a new GPU','Use an HDMI splitter','Connect one monitor to each port','Use a USB hub'],answer:2,explanation:'Most modern GPUs support multiple simultaneous display outputs. Simply connecting one monitor to the HDMI port and one to the DisplayPort enables dual-monitor setup without any additional hardware.'},
  {domain:'📱 Mobile Devices',q:'Which technology uses radio waves and allows devices within about 10 meters to communicate wirelessly?',options:['NFC','Wi-Fi','Bluetooth','Infrared'],answer:2,explanation:'Bluetooth operates at approximately 10 meters (Class 2 devices) using 2.4 GHz radio waves. It\'s used for peripherals like headsets, keyboards, and mice.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'What does NAT do?',options:['Assigns IP addresses automatically','Translates private IPs to a public IP for internet access','Encrypts network traffic','Filters packets based on rules'],answer:1,explanation:'NAT (Network Address Translation) allows multiple devices on a private network to share a single public IP address. The router translates private IPs to the public IP when sending to the internet.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A computer turns on but immediately shuts off. Which component is MOST likely causing this?',options:['Bad RAM','Overheating CPU','Corrupted OS','Failing GPU'],answer:1,explanation:'An immediate shutdown (within seconds of power-on, often before POST completes) is a classic sign of CPU overheating — usually due to thermal paste failure, unseated heatsink, or a stopped fan.'},
  {domain:'☁️ Virtualization',q:'Which of the following is a benefit of virtualization?',options:['Increased hardware requirements','Reduced power consumption','Slower application performance','Less isolation between systems'],answer:1,explanation:'Virtualization reduces physical server count, which directly reduces power consumption and cooling costs. Multiple VMs can run on one physical host, maximizing hardware utilization.'},
  {domain:'🔧 Troubleshooting',q:'After completing a repair, what should the technician ALWAYS do?',options:['Delete all event logs','Document the repair and educate the user','Reformat the drive','Return all original parts'],answer:1,explanation:'Step 6 of CompTIA\'s troubleshooting process requires verifying full functionality, documenting the solution, and educating the user to prevent recurrence. Documentation is critical for future support.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Which wireless encryption standard uses SAE (Simultaneous Authentication of Equals) for improved security?',options:['WEP','WPA','WPA2','WPA3'],answer:3,explanation:'WPA3 replaced WPA2\'s PSK (Pre-Shared Key) handshake with SAE (Simultaneous Authentication of Equals), which is resistant to offline dictionary attacks, making it significantly more secure.'},
  // Extra questions to reach 90
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'What is the function of a UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply)?',options:['Increases power efficiency','Provides backup power during outages to allow safe shutdown','Converts DC to AC power','Regulates voltage for overclocking'],answer:1,explanation:'A UPS contains a battery that provides immediate power when the main supply fails, giving enough time to save data and safely shut down systems. It also conditions power and protects against surges.'},
  {domain:'📱 Mobile Devices',q:'A technician needs to dispose of a laptop battery. What is the correct procedure?',options:['Throw in regular trash','Incinerate','Take to a battery recycling facility','Drain completely then discard normally'],answer:2,explanation:'Lithium batteries contain hazardous materials and cannot go in regular trash. They must be taken to a certified recycling facility or returned to a retailer with a battery recycling program.'},
  {domain:'🌐 Networking',q:'Which tool generates a tone that can be traced through walls using a probe?',options:['Cable tester','Toner probe','Loopback adapter','Network tap'],answer:1,explanation:'A toner (tone generator and probe) sends an audible signal through a cable. The probe detects this signal through walls and ceilings, helping identify which cable goes where — essential for infrastructure management.'},
  {domain:'🖥️ Hardware',q:'A laser printer is printing vertical lines on every page. What is the MOST likely cause?',options:['Low toner','Dirty fuser','Scratch on the drum','Paper jam residue'],answer:2,explanation:'Vertical lines or streaks on laser printer output are a classic symptom of a scratched or damaged photosensitive drum. The scratch causes toner to deposit incorrectly in that same spot on every page.'},
  {domain:'☁️ Virtualization',q:'Which of the following is an example of SaaS?',options:['Amazon EC2','Microsoft Azure VMs','Google Docs/Workspace','Docker containers'],answer:2,explanation:'Google Workspace (Gmail, Docs, Sheets) is SaaS — you just use the application without managing any infrastructure, platform, or software. EC2 and Azure VMs are IaaS. Docker is containerization, not a service model.'},
  {domain:'🔧 Troubleshooting',q:'A user reports that their printer is printing garbled text and random characters. What is MOST likely the cause?',options:['Bad paper','Corrupt print driver','Wrong paper size setting','Empty ink cartridge'],answer:1,explanation:'Garbled output (random characters, symbols, incorrect fonts) from a printer is almost always caused by a corrupt or incorrect print driver. Uninstalling and reinstalling the correct driver usually fixes this.'},
